### FEATURE_CHAT_ASSIST — turning a conversation you are in into a draft of the work it describes
###
### Every request here is a real one against a running instance. Sign in first: the session cookie and
### the cross-site token are what the chain expects.
###
### Ports: the demo backend runs on 8081 (Tomcat9 owns 8080 on this machine); the model is the
### `flowops-ollama` container on 11434. Start the backend with `--flowops.ai.enabled=true` or this
### feature answers `available: false` and nothing else, which is a supported configuration rather
### than a fault.
###
### **This is the only feature in the product that reads a message body for any purpose beyond showing
### it to the people in the conversation.** It exists under five binding conditions recorded in
### DECISION-CHAT-ASSIST-LOCAL-01, and three of them can be checked from this file alone:
###
###   1. It takes a conversation and no person. Participation comes from the session, so there is no
###      request that asks about somebody else's thread — see the 404 section at the foot.
###   2. The model is inside the installation. Point `flowops.ai.ollama-url` at anything that is not
###      and the application refuses to start, which is a louder answer than a runtime check.
###   3. Nothing is written. Ask twice, ask fifty times: no task, no process, no row saying you asked.
###
### The other two — nothing auto-applied, and the product supplying every word — are visible in the
### response: it carries a draft and no identifiers, and every `title` is a verbatim slice of the
### conversation.

@host = http://localhost:8081
@manager = ionut@atelier.ro
@stranger = cosmin@atelier.ro
@password = a-long-enough-passphrase

### Copy a conversation id out of the conversations list into this.
@conversationId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Sign in as somebody who is in the conversation.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{manager}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Your own conversations. Take an id from here — there is no route that lists anybody else's.
GET {{host}}/api/conversations

###############################################################################
### CHAT-ASSIST-SUGGEST-WORK-01 — the question
###############################################################################

### What work does this conversation describe? 200, with a draft or with nothing.
###
### On the seeded demonstration, the Aurora Coffee thread is the one to try: Ionuț says the retainer is
### signed and then names the whole engagement in one sentence — discovery workshop, competitor scan,
### positioning, messaging framework — in the order it happens, the way somebody actually types it.
###
### **Every `title` in the answer is a slice of that sentence.** The model points at phrases; the
### product looks them up and answers with the conversation's own characters. A phrase nobody typed is
### dropped, and if more than half the answer fails to check, the whole draft is suppressed — a draft
### assembled from the third of an answer that happened to be checkable is a different answer, one
### nobody produced.
POST {{host}}/api/chat-assist/conversations/{{conversationId}}/work-suggestion

### The same request again. **Nothing accumulates**, because nothing was written the first time.
### Compare the task count before and after if you want to see it rather than take it on trust.
POST {{host}}/api/chat-assist/conversations/{{conversationId}}/work-suggestion

### An empty list is an answer, and the commonest one.
###
### The seed writes a thread with no work in it — two people agreeing that Thursday suits them both.
### Ask about that one and the answer is `steps: []`. A model that found a process there would have
### found one that is not there, and the grounding rule is what stops it reaching anybody.

###############################################################################
### Where the draft goes
###############################################################################

### Nowhere, until a person sends it. The steps come back as words, and the composer that already
### exists — the one used to start a process from tasks — is what turns them into work, with every
### validation PROCESS applies and every refusal it makes.
###
### There is deliberately no endpoint here that creates anything. A route called
### `/work-suggestion/accept` would be this feature growing a way to write, which is the one thing
### DECISION-AI-NEVER-AUTO-APPLIES-01 and DECISION-CHAT-ASSIST-LOCAL-01 agree it must not have.

###############################################################################
### The refusal that is the whole guarantee
###############################################################################

### Sign in as somebody who is not in that conversation.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{stranger}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 404 — and it is the same 404 an invented identifier gives.
###
### **Told apart, these two answers would leak the workspace's conversations.** A caller who could tell
### *not yours* from *no such thing* could enumerate every thread in the business by trying identifiers,
### and learn who is talking to whom without reading a word. CHAT conflates them on its own routes and
### this one inherits the conflation by inheriting the exception.
POST {{host}}/api/chat-assist/conversations/{{conversationId}}/work-suggestion

### The same 404, for a conversation that does not exist. Compare the two responses: identical.
POST {{host}}/api/chat-assist/conversations/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111/work-suggestion

###############################################################################
### The honest limitation, to rehearse rather than avoid
###############################################################################

### A 3B model is unreliable at this. Measured while building the sibling feature: right every time on
### a clear handover, wrong about half the time on simple work. That is why the control is phrased as a
### question, why the draft is fully editable, and why an empty result is silence rather than an
### apology.
###
### If you are demonstrating this, ask the Aurora Coffee thread and the Thursday thread in that order.
### The second one is the more interesting answer.
